# handedOver(process)
# An argument puts `process` into hands nobody sees: whoever holds it may list its members and read each of them, so each counts as read, and what hangs on it in the table comes into the image.
# A receiver is only what a member was found on: store-under-a-key-nobody-knows-is-no-use-of-a-host-built-in.ir is that program
# LIBRARY: own
# RUN: valueflow-why used-builtin=ProcessSend used-builtin=ProcessChannel
# CHECK: used-builtin=ProcessSend
# CHECK-NOT: not held
# CHECK: used-builtin=ProcessChannel
# CHECK-NOT: not held

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="handedOver" [isFreeName]
    v2 = Builtin builtin=Process
    v3 = Call v1, -, v2
    Return
}
